            <ArticleTitle>Recurrent myocardial infarction provoked by multiple giant coronary aneurysms. A case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>311-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of multiple coronary aneurysms, complicated with repeated myocardial infarction, is presented. The cine-coronary angiogram and autopsy disclosed marked dilatation of epicardial coronary arteries associated with multiple giant thrombosed aneurysms, which is rare in patients with atherosclerosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
